    "ARP, elevation, magnetic variation, runway threshold coordinates, true bearings, threshold elevations, displaced thresholds, ILS (I-GG/I-WW 110.900) and ATS frequencies: UK AIP AD 2.EGKK (AD 2.2, 2.12, 2.18, 2.19), AIRAC 2610 (effective 01 OCT 2026).",
    "CTR polygon: AD 2.17 lateral limits with the 10 NM and 8 NM arcs densified every ~15 degrees.",
    "TIMBA and WILLO stacks (inbound true track, turn, FL070 minimum) from the RNAV hold coding table AD 2.EGKK-7-16.",
    "SIDs follow the RNAV1 SID coding tables AD 2.EGKK-6-18 to 6-22 (26L ...1X, 08R ...1Z/2Z), simplified to 3-4 of their waypoints; initial altitudes are the coded SID stop altitudes. KKxxx waypoint coordinates are from those tables.",
    "STARs follow the STAR coding tables AD 2.EGKK-7-10 to 7-14, simplified to 3-5 waypoints; entry altitudes are approximate (taken from the coded level constraints near the first fix).",
    "Runway 08L/26R is the standby runway (used only when 08R/26L is closed), so the configs use 08R/26L in mixed mode. inactiveRunways draws 08L/26R but routes it as a taxiway (AD 2.EGKK-2-1 hot spot HS1: aircraft vacating 26L cross 26R onto Juliet without a crossing clearance). Its AIP threshold data stays below for a future standby-runway config.",
    "holdRunways pins J1 and G1 (08R) and C1 (26L) to the runway they protect per the aerodrome chart AD 2.EGKK-2-1; their OSM positions are nearer the standby runway.",
    "OSM maps 08R/26L and 08L/26R threshold-to-threshold; mergeDisplacedThresholds folds the displaced-threshold ways back in so the take-off run starts at the real runway end.",
    "Fire station: centroid of the OSM 'Gatwick Airport Fire Station' building (approx). Airline -> terminal table is approximate (not in the AIP); easyJet uses both terminals and is listed under North.",
    "LON frequency 133.180 is the London Control frequency on the 26L BOGNA/HARDY SID chart (AD 2.EGKK-6-7)."
  ],
